DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  llooccaallee  command  displays information about the current locale, or
       all locales, on standard output.

       When invoked without arguments, llooccaallee displays the current locale set‐
       tings for each locale category (see llooccaallee(5)), based on  the  settings
       of  the  environment variables that control the locale (see llooccaallee(7)).
       Values for variables set in the environment are printed without  double
       quotes, implied values are printed with double quotes.

       If  either the --aa or the --mm option (or one of their long‐format equiva‐
       lents) is specified, the behavior is as follows:

       ----aallll--llooccaalleess
       --aa     Display a list of all available locales.  The --vv  option  causes
              the  LLCC__IIDDEENNTTIIFFIICCAATTIIOONN metadata about each locale to be included
              in the output.

       ----cchhaarrmmaappss
       --mm     Display  the  available  charmaps  (character  set   description
              files).   To  display  the current character set for the locale,
              use _l_o_c_a_l_e _-_c _c_h_a_r_m_a_p.

       The llooccaallee command can also be provided with  one  or  more  arguments,
       which  are  the  names  of  locale  keywords  (for  example,  _d_a_t_e___f_m_t,
       _c_t_y_p_e_-_c_l_a_s_s_-_n_a_m_e_s, _y_e_s_e_x_p_r, or _d_e_c_i_m_a_l___p_o_i_n_t) or locale categories (for
       example, LLCC__CCTTYYPPEE or LLCC__TTIIMMEE).  For each  argument,  the  following  is
       displayed:

       •  For a locale keyword, the value of that keyword to be displayed.

       •  For  a  locale category, the values of all keywords in that category
          are displayed.

       When arguments are supplied, the following options are meaningful:

       ----ccaatteeggoorryy--nnaammee
       --cc     For a category name argument, write the name of the locale cate‐
              gory on a separate line preceding the list of keyword values for
              that category.

              For a keyword name argument, write the name of the locale  cate‐
              gory  for  this keyword on a separate line preceding the keyword
              value.

              This option improves readability when  multiple  name  arguments
              are specified.  It can be combined with the --kk option.

       ----kkeeyywwoorrdd--nnaammee
       --kk     For  each  keyword  whose value is being displayed, include also
              the name of that keyword, so that the output has the format:

                  _k_e_y_w_o_r_d="_v_a_l_u_e"

       The llooccaallee command also knows about the following options:

       ----vveerrbboossee
       --vv     Display additional information for some command‐line option  and
              argument combinations.

       ----hheellpp
       --??     Display  a  summary  of  command‐line  options and arguments and
              exit.

       ----uussaaggee
              Display a short usage message and exit.

       ----vveerrssiioonn
       --VV     Display the program version and exit.

